# Private project libraries

This directory contains private libraries for this project.
PlatformIO compiles them into static libraries and links them into the executable file.

Put each library's source code in a separate directory (`lib/your_library_name/[Code]`).

This example shows the `Foo` and `Bar` libraries:

```text
|--lib
|  |
|  |--Bar
|  |  |--docs
|  |  |--examples
|  |  |--src
|  |     |- Bar.c
|  |     |- Bar.h
|  |  |- library.json (optional)
|  |
|  |--Foo
|  |  |- Foo.c
|  |  |- Foo.h
|  |
|  |- README --> THIS FILE
|
|- platformio.ini
|--src
   |- main.c
```

The optional `library.json` file sets custom build options and other library settings.
See the [PlatformIO library configuration reference](https://docs.platformio.org/page/librarymanager/config.html).

Example contents of `src/main.c` with Foo and Bar:

```
#include <Foo.h>
#include <Bar.h>

int main (void)
{
  ...
}

```

The PlatformIO Library Dependency Finder scans project source files to find library dependencies automatically.
See the [Library Dependency Finder documentation](https://docs.platformio.org/page/librarymanager/ldf.html) for more information.
